  "limitations": "The selected body or finger collision trace axis changes, with exact P2 body interpolation and exact linear rigid finger interpolation onto unchanged bulk unknowns. Reference geometry/initializer anchors are byte-identical, and original physical material/mass, finger meshes/axes/masses, controls, dt, friction and barrier range remain fixed. Each case independently resolves its original held initializer. Undeformed actual surface areas are checked by group; deformed surface and active lumped support can change. Opposite finger reactions identify source wrenches, not continuum contact islands. Force-density norms use discrete nodal forces divided by positive lumped sample areas, not a continuous pressure reconstruction. Normal-contact rotation invariance is checked separately; total frictional surface moment is measured without imposing an additional zero-moment acceptance gate on the existing finite-gap, lagged-tangent friction law. One final common-time comparison isolates this contact-integration axis conditionally on the fixed bulk/geometry and regularization; it does not establish bulk/geometry convergence, full histories/application, model/feedback accuracy or verified warmed cost."
